## Findings and fixes (both in bf7af37d4, gate script only; no app code change)

- F410 [Nit] FIX. Cause: the `extraSelector` speaker branch of `allControlsAtLandscape`
  had never run on a failing page — `TILE_LABEL_AUDIO` is empty, so `speakers_found=0`
  today, and the only self-tests called the function without the probe, so a defect in
  the branch (a wrong selector, a bad rect filter, a wrong edge) would stay hidden until
  the first tile recording ships. Fix: the `/audio-below-fold` self-test page (a 600 px
  block, then one `<audio controls>` with a fixed 300x54 box) is measured with
  `allControlsAtLandscape(p, 'button', 'audio')`, and the row rule must reject the page.
  Recorded self-test output: `selftest all_controls_speaker_probe=false
  (speakers_found=1, speakers_outside=1, speaker_bottom_px=662, viewport_px=390)` — the
  branch reports the outside speaker and the rule fails, so the branch is no longer
  untested.
- F411 [Nit] FIX. Cause: the song `all_controls_visible` minimum of 1 equals the fallback
  `WeekHomeLink`, so a week with no song passed the row on one link (A4 class). Fix: the
  song row's open step requires a `section[data-part="song"] button` and throws when
  absent, as the end-of-book and question rows do. Self-test on the fallback page
  (`/one-link`, one link, no song section):
  `selftest all_controls_song_open song_open_ok=false count_rule_ok=true
  (controls_found=1, controls_min=1, song_buttons_found=0)` — the fallback passes the
  count rule and fails the open rule, so the row fails on a missing song. The plan Turn
  15 block holds a `Correction (turn 16, F411):` line instead of a history rewrite.

